      <Desc>Public Health Research and Development consists of the following: The Tobacco-Related Disease Research Program TRDRP aims to eliminate commercial tobacco use and tobacco-related diseases and to improve the health and well-being of all Californians. The Centers for Disease Control and Prevention uses blood collection to create newborn quality assurance materials and improve newborn screening laboratory methods. The U.S. Environmental Protection Agency conducts ambient air monitoring of pollutants of greatest concern in communities with environmental and health outcome disparities stemming from pollution and the COVID-19 pandemic. The National Institutes of Health conducts research on the effects of multigenerational air pollution exposure on adverse birth outcomes.</Desc>
